{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01LekuLTf1otgEmx6c1u9B1k","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed imagined/predicted experimental results for each planned experiment in the experiment plan, based on the \"median\" tier definition provided in Phase 1. I need to produce a single YAML block with all the predictions and rationales.\n\nLet me carefully go through each experiment and predict what results would look like in the median tier scenario.\n\nKey median tier characteristics:\n- Only LAMBADA + 1 extra task shows convergence, rest no significant trend\n- 7B models unavailable or only partial\n- Excluding GDN weakens convergence but direction holds (CI widens but doesn't cross zero)\n\n\n- Per-example Jaccard stays below 0.15, though the extra task paradox isn't as pronounced\n- The 340M rebound is explainable but lacks quantitative rigor\n- Only 1-2 tasks demonstrate significant convergence patterns\n- LAMBADA shows 50-75% standard deviation reduction\n- Spearman correlation at 1.3B ranges from -0.95 to -0.8\n- Pairwise Jaccard falls between 0.08-0.18\n- Bootstrap confidence interval lower bounds for std reduction sit at 0.001-0.01\n- I have 2 scale points to work with\n- Sample characterization reveals 1-2 significant features\n\nNow I'm mapping each experiment to its predicted results under this median tier scenario.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9617,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9617},"output_tokens":23,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5d2e06b4-f4d5-422a-a624-6c6aadf43447","uuid":"cf939b5d-dd1b-47e7-aa20-c2430043bdfd"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01LekuLTf1otgEmx6c1u9B1k","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Claim 1收窄为\"retrieval-dependent tasks上的convergence\"，不再claim泛化性。\n  Claim 2从\"scale-dependent convergence\"改为\"binary contrast: 340M insufficient vs 1.3B sufficient\"，\n  承认无法建立完整scale law但指出threshold现象。\n  Claim 3（paradox）仍是核心卖点，但限定在LAMBADA上做深度案例研究。\n  Title加限定词如\"on retrieval-dependent tasks\"。目标：EMNLP 2026 Findings（Main边缘）。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Cross-task convergence quantification\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      对6个benchmark在1.3B和340M上计算cross-architecture std随attention ratio的变化趋势，\n      Spearman相关检验，并按retrieval-dependent vs reasoning-dependent分类task。\n    expected_results:\n      lambada_std_h0_to_h8_1_3b: [0.024, 0.005]\n      lambada_spearman_rho_1_3b: -0.90\n      lambada_spearman_p_1_3b: 0.037\n      hellaswag_std_h0_to_h8_1_3b: [0.018, 0.011]\n      hellaswag_spearman_rho_1_3b: -0.82\n      hellaswag_spearman_p_1_3b: 0.089\n      arc_easy_std_h0_to_h8_1_3b: [0.015, 0.013]\n      arc_easy_spearman_rho_1_3b: -0.30\n      arc_easy_spearman_p_1_3b: 0.624\n      arc_challenge_std_h0_to_h8_1_3b: [0.022, 0.019]\n      arc_challenge_spearman_rho_1_3b: -0.10\n      arc_challenge_spearman_p_1_3b: 0.873\n      piqa_std_h0_to_h8_1_3b: [0.011, 0.010]\n      piqa_spearman_rho_1_3b: -0.20\n      piqa_spearman_p_1_3b: 0.747\n      winogrande_std_h0_to_h8_1_3b: [0.016, 0.014]\n      winogrande_spearman_rho_1_3b: -0.50\n      winogrande_spearman_p_1_3b: 0.391\n      tasks_with_p_lt_0_05: 1\n      tasks_with_p_lt_0_10: 2\n      lambada_std_reduction_pct: 79\n      hellaswag_std_reduction_pct: 39\n    result_rationale: >\n      LAMBADA是high retrieval demand的cloze task——模型必须从长context中\"检索\"关键信息来预测最后一个词。\n      加入attention后，所有架构都能更有效地执行这种long-range retrieval，因此各架构的性能天花板趋同，\n      cross-arch std显著下降（ρ=-0.90, p=0.037）。HellaSwag有一定的retrieval成分（需要从premise推断continuation），\n      但同时涉及commonsense reasoning，因此convergence趋势弱于LAMBADA（ρ=-0.82但p=0.089，刚好不够显著）。\n      ARC、PIQA、Winogrande主要考察reasoning和world knowledge，这些能力更依赖于base recurrence的训练质量而非\n      attention带来的retrieval能力提升，因此attention并不能消除架构间的固有差异，std几乎不变。\n      这构成了一个清晰的task-type dichotomy：retrieval-dependent tasks收敛，reasoning tasks不收敛。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 1: Cross-architecture std reduction by benchmark (1.3B scale)\"\n        columns: [\"Benchmark\", \"Task Type\", \"Std (h=0)\", \"Std (h=8)\", \"Reduction %\", \"Spearman ρ\", \"p-value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LAMBADA\", \"Retrieval\", \"0.024\", \"0.005\", \"79%\", \"-0.90\", \"0.037*\"]\n          - [\"HellaSwag\", \"Retrieval+Reasoning\", \"0.018\", \"0.011\", \"39%\", \"-0.82\", \"0.089†\"]\n          - [\"ARC-Easy\", \"Reasoning\", \"0.015\", \"0.013\", \"13%\", \"-0.30\", \"0.624\"]\n          - [\"ARC-Challenge\", \"Reasoning\", \"0.022\", \"0.019\", \"14%\", \"-0.10\", \"0.873\"]\n          - [\"PIQA\", \"Reasoning\", \"0.011\", \"0.010\", \"9%\", \"-0.20\", \"0.747\"]\n          - [\"WinoGrande\", \"Reasoning\", \"0.016\", \"0.014\", \"13%\", \"-0.50\", \"0.391\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 1: 6-panel grid，每个benchmark一个panel。x轴attention ratio (0,1,3,5,8)，y轴cross-arch std。LAMBADA panel展示清晰下降曲线，HellaSwag有弱下降趋势，其余4个基本flat。灰色shaded区域标注'retrieval-dependent zone'。\"\n    analysis: >\n      仅LAMBADA通过p<0.05显著性检验，HellaSwag在p<0.10边缘。这支持将Claim 1收窄为retrieval-dependent tasks。\n      Dichotomy本身是一个有意义的发现——说明attention的equalizer effect具有task-specificity，\n      而非universally homogenizing。论文叙事可以将此framing为\"attention selectively equalizes retrieval\n      but not reasoning\"，这比universal claim弱但更精确、更defensible。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark per-example analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      对1.3B模型在HellaSwag、ARC-easy、ARC-challenge上用--log_samples重新跑lm-eval，\n      提取per-example accuracy变化，计算sample-level convergence和cross-architecture helped/hurt overlap。\n    expected_results:\n      hellaswag_pairwise_jaccard_helped: 0.14\n      hellaswag_pairwise_jaccard_hurt: 0.11\n      hellaswag_net_effect_gdn: -0.008\n      hellaswag_net_effect_retnet: -0.003\n      hellaswag_net_effect_hgrn2: 0.012\n      hellaswag_symmetric_paradox_strength: \"weak\"\n      arc_easy_pairwise_jaccard_helped: 0.22\n      arc_easy_convergence_pattern: \"absent\"\n      arc_challenge_pairwise_jaccard_helped: 0.19\n      arc_challenge_convergence_pattern: \"absent\"\n      gpu_hours_used: 7.5\n    result_rationale: >\n      HellaSwag上per-example分析会显示一定程度的paradox——helped/hurt样本跨架构的Jaccard仍然较低（0.11-0.14），\n      说明不同架构在不同样本上受益/受损，但效果不如LAMBADA干净：(1) HellaSwag是4选1的multiple-choice，\n      accuracy是discrete的0/1，不像LAMBADA的连续logprob那样能捕捉细粒度变化，这导致noise更大；\n      (2) net effect的asymmetry不如LAMBADA对称——GDN和RetNet被hurt的程度不同，HGRN2被help的程度也较小，\n      paradox的\"symmetric but opposite\"叙事在HellaSwag上不够compelling。\n      ARC-easy和ARC-challenge因为aggregate level就没有convergence，per-example level自然也没有一致的pattern——\n      Jaccard偏高（0.19-0.22）反映的是随机重叠而非systematic pattern。\n      这个结果支持将paradox深度分析限定在LAMBADA，HellaSwag作为supporting evidence但不作为核心claim。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 2: Per-example overlap analysis across benchmarks (1.3B, h3→h8)\"\n        columns: [\"Benchmark\", \"Jaccard (helped)\", \"Jaccard (hurt)\", \"GDN net\", \"RetNet net\", \"HGRN2 net\", \"Paradox clarity\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LAMBADA\", \"0.08\", \"0.06\", \"-0.031\", \"-0.018\", \"+0.027\", \"Strong\"]\n          - [\"HellaSwag\", \"0.14\", \"0.11\", \"-0.008\", \"-0.003\", \"+0.012\", \"Weak\"]\n          - [\"ARC-Easy\", \"0.22\", \"0.20\", \"+0.002\", \"-0.005\", \"+0.001\", \"None\"]\n          - [\"ARC-Challenge\", \"0.19\", \"0.17\", \"-0.003\", \"+0.001\", \"-0.002\", \"None\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 2: 2×2 panel。上排LAMBADA和HellaSwag的upset plot展示helped/hurt样本跨架构的overlap；下排对应的net effect bar chart。LAMBADA panel颜色对比鲜明（GDN/RetNet红色hurt vs HGRN2绿色help），HellaSwag panel对比较弱。\"\n    analysis: >\n      HellaSwag提供了部分supporting evidence——Jaccard低于random baseline说明architecture-specificity存在，\n      但net effect不够对称，paradox叙事不clean。ARC两个task完全没有pattern。\n      实际操作：论文中LAMBADA做完整deep dive（主图+主表），HellaSwag放在supplementary作为partial replication，\n      ARC作为negative control说明effect的task-specificity。这比只有LAMBADA的单task故事更robust。\n\n  - name: \"7B model evaluation (if available)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      检查Wang et al. HuggingFace repos中7B模型的可用性。如果可用则评估，如果不可用则加强340M的two-scale分析。\n    expected_results:\n      gdn_7b_available: false\n      retnet_7b_available: true\n      hgrn2_7b_available: false\n      complete_7b_trio: false\n      fallback_triggered: true\n      fallback_action: \"strengthen 2-scale binary contrast analysis\"\n      scale_points_available: 2\n    result_rationale: >\n      Wang et al.的model zoo主要集中在340M和1.3B规模——7B训练需要显著更多compute（约8×），\n      他们可能只对部分架构训练了7B。RetNet因为是相对成熟的架构（微软支持），最可能有7B版本，\n      但GDN和HGRN2作为较新的架构，7B训练可能未完成或未release。\n      只有一个架构的7B数据无法计算cross-architecture std，因此无法构成三点scale curve。\n      Fallback策略：将Claim 2重新框架为binary contrast——340M是\"insufficient scale\"（convergence partial，\n      有rebound），1.3B是\"sufficient scale\"（convergence complete）。这不是一个scale law，\n      而是一个threshold observation。叙事上诚实承认\"we cannot establish the full scaling trajectory\"，\n      但指出threshold的存在本身有practical implications（practitioners知道1.3B足够触发convergence）。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 3（修改版）: 不再画三点scale curve，而是side-by-side的两个panel——340M和1.3B各一个，每个panel内画cross-arch std vs attention ratio。用箭头和annotation标注'partial convergence with rebound'(340M) vs 'complete convergence'(1.3B)。\"\n    analysis: >\n      7B不可用是median tier最大的narrative限制。无法用三点建立scale law意味着Claim 2从quantitative scaling claim\n      降级为qualitative threshold observation。但binary contrast本身在empirical paper中是可接受的——\n      关键是要坦诚acknowledge limitation并在discussion中指出7B验证是important future work。\n      如果RetNet单独有7B，可以在appendix中报告\"single-architecture 7B data point consistent with trend\"，\n      但不能claim cross-architecture convergence at 7B。\n\n  - name: \"340M rebound mechanism analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007\"\n    description: >\n      深入分析340M在attn=8时的non-monotonic rebound——per-example比较340M与1.3B在相同attention ratio下的行为差异。\n    expected_results:\n      rebound_magnitude_std_increase_h5_to_h8: 0.008\n      rebound_primary_source: \"GDN disproportionate degradation at h=8\"\n      rebound_sample_overlap_with_1_3b_hurt: 0.35\n      capacity_limitation_hypothesis_support: \"moderate\"\n      gdn_340m_h8_accuracy_drop_vs_h5: -0.028\n      retnet_340m_h8_accuracy_drop_vs_h5: -0.009\n      hgrn2_340m_h8_accuracy_change_vs_h5: +0.004\n      identified_mechanism: \"capacity bottleneck — at 340M, replacing too many recurrent layers with attention leaves insufficient recurrent capacity for sequence modeling, hitting GDN hardest due to its higher recurrent parameter efficiency\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      340M模型的total parameter budget有限。当attention ratio从h=5增加到h=8时，大量recurrent层被替换为attention层。\n      在1.3B规模下，剩余的recurrent层仍有足够capacity处理sequence modeling，但在340M下，\n      recurrent层的capacity被过度压缩。GDN的gated delta rule机制对参数效率最敏感——\n      它依赖于gate和delta的精确交互，参数减少导致这种交互退化最严重。\n      RetNet基于exponential decay的机制相对robust但也受影响。HGRN2的hierarchical结构天然对capacity减少有一定resilience。\n      Per-example分析中，340M rebound处受影响的样本与1.3B被hurt的样本overlap只有0.35——\n      说明rebound不是简单的\"same problem at smaller scale\"，而是340M特有的capacity limitation触发了不同failure mode。\n      这个解释合理但缺乏formal quantitative validation（如information bottleneck分析），因此标注为\"moderate support\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 3: 340M rebound decomposition (h=5 → h=8)\"\n        columns: [\"Architecture\", \"Acc@h5\", \"Acc@h8\", \"Δ\", \"Cross-arch std contribution\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GDN\", \"0.412\", \"0.384\", \"-0.028\", \"↑ major\"]\n          - [\"RetNet\", \"0.398\", \"0.389\", \"-0.009\", \"↑ minor\"]\n          - [\"HGRN2\", \"0.405\", \"0.409\", \"+0.004\", \"↓ minor\"]\n          - [\"Cross-arch std\", \"0.007\", \"0.013\", \"+0.006\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 4: 左panel为340M三架构accuracy随attention ratio的曲线，h=8处GDN明显下弯；右panel为scatter plot展示340M rebound样本vs 1.3B hurt样本的overlap（low Jaccard）。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Capacity limitation假设提供了合理解释但不是定量严格的。论文中将此作为\"interesting secondary finding\"处理——\n      在Results中用一小节描述，在Discussion中作为evidence支持\"convergence requires sufficient scale\"的论点。\n      不过不要过度claim因果关系，用\"consistent with\"而非\"demonstrates\"的语言。\n\n  - name: \"Helped/hurt sample characterization\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      对LAMBADA上各架构的helped/hurt样本计算target token frequency、context length、last-sentence complexity等特征，\n      检验是否有显著差异。\n    expected_results:\n      target_token_frequency_p_value_helped_vs_hurt: 0.003\n      target_token_frequency_effect_direction: \"hurt samples have lower-frequency target tokens\"\n      target_token_frequency_cohens_d: 0.38\n      context_length_p_value_helped_vs_hurt: 0.12\n      context_length_effect_direction: \"weak trend — hurt samples slightly longer\"\n      last_sentence_perplexity_p_value: 0.067\n      cross_architecture_feature_difference_significant: true\n      gdn_hurt_skew: \"low-frequency targets with medium context\"\n      retnet_hurt_skew: \"low-frequency targets with long context\"\n      hgrn2_helped_skew: \"low-frequency targets across context lengths\"\n      significant_features_count: 1\n      marginally_significant_features_count: 1\n    result_rationale: >\n      Target token frequency是最可能显著的特征，因为retrieval-dependent prediction的核心难度在于target token的可预测性。\n      低频词更难预测，attention的加入对不同架构在这类样本上的影响不同：\n      - GDN的delta rule机制擅长精确的key-value关联，加入attention后在低频目标上反而产生interference（两种attention机制竞争）\n      - RetNet的exponential decay对长distance retrieval本来就弱，attention在长context+低频target上无法完全补偿\n      - HGRN2的hierarchical gating从attention中获益最多，因为它的base mechanism最缺乏long-range retrieval能力\n      Context length效果不显著（p=0.12）可能因为LAMBADA样本的context length变化范围有限（多数在50-200 tokens之间），\n      不足以产生统计显著的差异。Last-sentence perplexity在边缘（p=0.067）。\n      Cross-architecture差异在target frequency上显著——三个架构的hurt样本都倾向low-frequency targets，\n      但具体的frequency threshold和与context length的交互pattern不同，这解释了为什么Jaccard低。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 4: Sample feature analysis — helped vs hurt on LAMBADA (1.3B, h0→h8)\"\n        columns: [\"Feature\", \"Helped mean\", \"Hurt mean\", \"Cohen's d\", \"p-value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Target token log-freq\", \"-5.2\", \"-6.8\", \"0.38\", \"0.003**\"]\n          - [\"Context length (tokens)\", \"87.3\", \"94.1\", \"0.15\", \"0.12\"]\n          - [\"Last-sent perplexity\", \"42.1\", \"51.8\", \"0.21\", \"0.067†\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 5: 三行（GDN/RetNet/HGRN2）×两列（target freq distribution / context length distribution）的violin plot。Helped样本蓝色，hurt样本红色。Target frequency列上三架构都显示shift但shift pattern不同。\"\n    analysis: >\n      仅1个特征（target token frequency）达到strong significance，1个marginally significant。这符合median tier预期。\n      Target frequency作为单一显著特征足以构成一个coherent story：attention的equalizer effect主要作用在\n      低频target token的retrieval上，但不同架构对这类样本的处理策略不同。\n      论文中可以用这个结果支持Claim 3的mechanistic interpretation——\"convergence through complementary mechanisms\"\n      有了具体的linguistic grounding（不同架构在不同frequency regime的低频tokens上diverge）。\n      Limitation：只有1-2个显著特征意味着mechanistic story不够多维度，reviewer可能要求更多特征。\n      准备rebuttal：(a) LAMBADA样本本身的feature空间较窄，(b) frequency是retrieval task最relevant的特征。\n\n  - name: \"Attention weight extraction and visualization\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: >\n      提取三个架构hybrid model (h3-1 config)的attention weight，分析attention pattern与per-example effect的关系。\n    expected_results:\n      attention_pattern_similarity_gdn_retnet: 0.42\n      attention_pattern_similarity_gdn_hgrn2: 0.31\n      attention_pattern_similarity_retnet_hgrn2: 0.38\n      correlation_attention_entropy_with_helped: 0.28\n      correlation_attention_focus_position_with_effect: 0.33\n      qualitative_finding: \"GDN attention concentrates on recent context; RetNet distributes more uniformly; HGRN2 shows bimodal pattern with peaks at sentence boundaries\"\n      gpu_hours_used: 3.5\n    result_rationale: >\n      三种base recurrence机制对信息的编码方式不同，这会影响attention层\"看到\"的hidden states的distribution，\n      进而导致不同的attention pattern。GDN通过delta rule维护explicit key-value memory，\n      attention层在这个基础上倾向于做local refinement（集中在recent context）；\n      RetNet的exponential decay平滑了positional信息，attention分布更uniform；\n      HGRN2的hierarchical gating创造了sentence-boundary处的natural segmentation，\n      attention倾向于在这些boundary处聚焦。\n      Attention entropy与helped/hurt的相关性中等（r=0.28-0.33），因为attention weight只是机制的一个proxy，\n      实际效果还取决于value vector的内容和后续层的处理。\n      这些相关性达不到pass_fail threshold（>0.3）的一部分，但focus position的相关性（0.33）刚好过线。\n      整体来说提供了supportive但非conclusive的mechanistic evidence。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 5: Cross-architecture attention pattern analysis (h3-1, 1.3B)\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"GDN\", \"RetNet\", \"HGRN2\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Mean attention entropy\", \"1.82\", \"2.45\", \"2.11\"]\n          - [\"% attention on last 20 tokens\", \"48%\", \"29%\", \"35%\"]\n          - [\"Correlation with helped (r)\", \"0.28\", \"0.25\", \"0.33\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 6: 三个architecture的average attention heatmap（x轴=query position, y轴=key position），各展示不同的attention pattern。下方bar chart展示与per-example effect的correlation。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Attention pattern分析提供了定性的mechanistic支持——三个架构确实展现出不同的attention策略，\n      与per-example divergence的发现一致。但相关性不够强，不足以claim causal mechanism。\n      论文中放在supplementary或作为一个小节提供visual evidence，不作为核心argument。\n      这对median tier来说是合适的——有一些mechanistic insight但不deep enough for a full claim。\n\n  - name: \"Architecture expansion check\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      搜索Wang et al. model zoo和其他source寻找额外的hybrid architectures（Mamba/Mamba2, RWKV等），\n      评估convergence是否泛化。\n    expected_results:\n      mamba2_hybrid_found: false\n      rwkv_hybrid_found: false\n      additional_architectures_evaluated: 0\n      wang_et_al_architectures_confirmed: [\"GDN\", \"RetNet\", \"HGRN2\"]\n      other_sources_checked: [\"HuggingFace Hub\", \"Papers with Code\", \"GitHub\"]\n      conclusion: \"no additional comparable hybrid architectures available with matching scale/ratio configurations\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Wang et al.的model zoo是目前最全面的hybrid architecture比较资源。他们选择的三个架构（GDN, RetNet, HGRN2）\n      已经覆盖了主要的linear recurrence类型。Mamba/Mamba2的hybrid版本虽然存在于一些研究中，\n      但没有以相同的scale（340M/1.3B）和attention ratio（0,1,3,5,8层）系统训练并release的checkpoint。\n      RWKV hybrid更是一个新兴方向，公开的comparable checkpoints几乎没有。\n      这意味着我们stuck在n=3架构——但这三个架构确实代表了三种不同的recurrence mechanism，\n      不是arbitrary的架构选择。论文中需要在limitation section说明这一点。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      无法扩展架构数量。Mitigation：(1) 在方法论上强调三个架构代表三类不同的recurrence paradigm，\n      (2) 引用Wang et al.选择这三个架构的justification，(3) 在limitation中explicitly call out n=3，\n      (4) 指出每个架构×5 ratios×2 scales的per-example analysis提供了thousands of data points。\n      对于EMNLP Findings来说，n=3但per-example analysis deep的paper是可接受的。\n\n  - name: \"Statistical robustness framework\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      Bootstrap CI、多重比较校正、排除GDN的sensitivity analysis、effect sizes。\n    expected_results:\n      bootstrap_ci_lambada_std_reduction_95: [0.004, 0.021]\n      bootstrap_ci_lower_bound_positive: true\n      bootstrap_ci_hellaswag_std_reduction_95: [-0.002, 0.015]\n      bootstrap_ci_hellaswag_lower_crosses_zero: true\n      bonferroni_corrected_p_lambada: 0.222\n      fdr_corrected_p_lambada: 0.074\n      fdr_corrected_p_hellaswag: 0.267\n      gdn_excluded_lambada_spearman_rho: -0.80\n      gdn_excluded_lambada_spearman_p: 0.133\n      gdn_excluded_bootstrap_ci_std_reduction: [0.001, 0.018]\n      gdn_excluded_ci_crosses_zero: false\n      cohens_d_lambada_convergence: 0.72\n      eta_squared_attention_ratio_effect: 0.41\n    result_rationale: >\n      Bootstrap CI对LAMBADA的std reduction不跨零（[0.004, 0.021]），确认convergence是real的。\n      但CI相当宽，反映了n=3架构带来的有限统计power。\n      HellaSwag的bootstrap CI跨零（[-0.002, 0.015]），与exp-001中p=0.089一致——borderline。\n      Bonferroni correction对6个benchmarks（×6）后LAMBADA的p值从0.037变为0.222——不再显著。\n      但FDR correction（less conservative）给出0.074，接近显著。这里的tension需要在论文中诚实讨论——\n      如果用strict Bonferroni全都不显著，但Bonferroni在correlated tests上过于conservative。\n      FDR更appropriate但仍只是borderline。解决方案：focus on LAMBADA的pre-registered hypothesis（不需correction），\n      其他tasks作为exploratory analysis用FDR。\n      排除GDN后：direction保持（ρ=-0.80）但p值变大（0.133），因为只剩两个架构（RetNet, HGRN2），\n      permutation test的resolution有限。关键是bootstrap CI仍不跨零（[0.001, 0.018]）——\n      CI下界接近零但还是正的，说明convergence方向在没有GDN的情况下依然成立，只是不够显著。\n      Cohen's d=0.72属于medium-to-large effect，说明convergence不是trivial的。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 6: Statistical robustness summary\"\n        columns: [\"Analysis\", \"LAMBADA\", \"HellaSwag\", \"Others\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Raw Spearman p\", \"0.037*\", \"0.089†\", \">0.39\"]\n          - [\"Bonferroni-corrected p\", \"0.222\", \"0.534\", \">1.0\"]\n          - [\"FDR-corrected p\", \"0.074†\", \"0.267\", \">0.58\"]\n          - [\"Bootstrap 95% CI (std reduction)\", \"[0.004, 0.021]\", \"[-0.002, 0.015]\", \"all cross zero\"]\n          - [\"GDN-excluded bootstrap CI\", \"[0.001, 0.018]\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Cohen's d\", \"0.72\", \"0.34\", \"<0.2\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 7: Forest plot展示各benchmark的bootstrap CI。LAMBADA的CI在正区间，HellaSwag刚好跨零，其余clearly跨零。右侧panel展示GDN-excluded的sensitivity analysis CI。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Robustness analysis的结论是nuanced的：LAMBADA的convergence是robust的（CI不跨零，medium-large effect size），\n      但statistical significance在multiple comparison correction后变弱。\n      排除GDN后direction preserved但CI下界接近零——这是honest reporting，reviewer会appreciate这种transparency。\n      论文策略：(1) Pre-register LAMBADA为primary hypothesis，avoid multiple comparison问题，\n      (2) 报告FDR而非Bonferroni（justification：tasks are correlated），\n      (3) GDN sensitivity作为robustness check而非primary analysis，\n      (4) 强调effect size（d=0.72）而非仅rely on p-value。\n      这种nuanced statistical picture对EMNLP Findings是sufficient的——不pretend effect比实际更强。\n\n  - name: \"Wang et al. explicit differentiation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      正式的side-by-side比较：Wang et al.报告了什么，我们的分析新增了什么。\n    expected_results:\n      wang_convergence_statements_found: 2\n      wang_statement_1: \"qualitative observation that hybrid models show similar performance at higher attention ratios\"\n      wang_statement_2: \"aggregate benchmark tables showing decreasing variance (not explicitly computed or tested)\"\n      differentiation_point_1: \"We compute cross-architecture std trajectories with statistical tests — they don't\"\n      differentiation_point_2: \"We perform per-example analysis revealing the equalizer paradox — they don't\"\n      differentiation_point_3: \"We characterize scale dependency of convergence (340M partial vs 1.3B complete) — they don't\"\n      differentiation_point_4: \"We provide mechanistic analysis linking sample features to architecture-specific effects — they don't\"\n      wang_overlap_risk: \"moderate — a reviewer familiar with their paper will see the qualitative convergence trend in their tables\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Wang et al.的论文focus是建model zoo和benchmark hybrid architectures的aggregate performance。\n      他们在论文中很可能提到了\"increasing attention leads to similar performance across architectures\"\n      作为一个observation，但没有将其作为核心finding来quantify或analyze。\n      他们的Table/Figure中确实隐含了convergence趋势（读者可以从数字中看出来），但他们没有：\n      (a) 计算cross-arch std并测试其与attention ratio的关系，\n      (b) 做任何per-example分析，\n      (c) 区分不同scale下convergence的不同程度，\n      (d) 分析为什么convergence发生。\n      Risk在于reviewer可能认为\"convergence observation已经在Wang et al.中了\"——mitigation是\n      明确acknowledge他们的qualitative observation并frame our contribution为将这个observation\n      从qualitative提升到quantitative+mechanistic。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 7: Differentiation from Wang et al. (2025)\"\n        columns: [\"Analysis dimension\", \"Wang et al.\", \"Our work\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Convergence observation\", \"Qualitative (implicit in tables)\", \"Quantitative (Spearman tests, effect sizes)\"]\n          - [\"Per-example analysis\", \"None\", \"Helped/hurt decomposition, Jaccard overlap\"]\n          - [\"Scale dependency\", \"Not analyzed\", \"340M partial vs 1.3B complete, rebound mechanism\"]\n          - [\"Mechanistic analysis\", \"None\", \"Sample characterization, attention pattern analysis\"]\n          - [\"Statistical framework\", \"None\", \"Bootstrap CI, sensitivity analysis, multiple comparison\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Differentiation清晰但需要careful framing。在Introduction中：acknowledge Wang et al.的model zoo贡献，\n      然后explicit说\"building on their excellent resource, we discover and characterize...\"。\n      在Related Work中：detailed comparison table。避免任何暗示他们\"missed\"something的语言——\n      frame为\"their focus was X, ours is complementary Y\"。\n      Risk assessment：如果Wang et al.的reviewer也review我们的paper（likely given community size），\n      他们可能defensive。Respectful framing essential。\n\n  - name: \"Convergence-divergence bridge analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-010\"\n    description: >\n      在LAMBADA上同时plot aggregate convergence和per-example divergence metrics，展示paradox的co-evolution。\n    expected_results:\n      correlation_aggregate_std_vs_jaccard: -0.88\n      correlation_p_value: 0.048\n      aggregate_std_trajectory: [0.024, 0.019, 0.012, 0.008, 0.005]\n      mean_pairwise_jaccard_trajectory: [0.15, 0.12, 0.10, 0.08, 0.07]\n      net_effect_asymmetry_trajectory: [0.008, 0.015, 0.021, 0.025, 0.031]\n      paradox_intensification_with_attention: true\n      effect_asymmetry_correlation_with_attention_ratio: 0.95\n    result_rationale: >\n      随着attention ratio增加，aggregate convergence加强（std下降）同时per-example divergence也在加强\n      （Jaccard下降、net effect asymmetry增加）。这是因为更多的attention层给了每个架构更大的\"空间\"\n      来发展architecture-specific的processing策略——base recurrence mechanism决定了哪些sample被route到attention，\n      而更多的attention层意味着这种architecture-specific routing的影响被放大。\n      Aggregate convergence的同时出现是因为这些不同策略恰好\"平均化\"到similar的overall performance——\n      这不是coincidence而是因为attention的通用retrieval能力设定了一个performance ceiling，\n      不同架构通过不同路径reach这个ceiling。\n      Correlation为-0.88（p=0.048）——刚好显著。这是paradox的quantitative visualization。\n      Net effect asymmetry（|GDN_net| + |RetNet_net| + |HGRN2_net|）随attention ratio单调增加，\n      correlation 0.95——说明per-example effects变得更pronounced even as aggregate converges。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 8: Convergence-divergence co-evolution on LAMBADA (1.3B)\"\n        columns: [\"Attention layers\", \"Cross-arch std\", \"Mean pairwise Jaccard\", \"Net effect asymmetry\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"0 (pure recurrent)\", \"0.024\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"1\", \"0.019\", \"0.12\", \"0.015\"]\n          - [\"3\", \"0.012\", \"0.10\", \"0.021\"]\n          - [\"5\", \"0.008\", \"0.08\", \"0.025\"]\n          - [\"8\", \"0.005\", \"0.07\", \"0.031\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 8 (论文核心图): Dual-axis plot。左y轴为cross-arch std（下降曲线，蓝色），右y轴为net effect asymmetry（上升曲线，红色）。x轴为attention层数。两条曲线形成'X'形交叉，视觉化paradox。下方small multiples展示各attention ratio下的pairwise Jaccard heatmap逐渐变冷（overlap减少）。\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是论文的\"money figure\"——一张图capture整个paradox。Dual-axis plot清晰展示aggregate convergence和\n      per-example divergence的co-evolution。Correlation显著（p=0.048）但不是overwhelmingly strong，\n      符合median tier。\n      Narrative：这张图支撑整个Section 4（或5）的核心argument——\"attention creates convergence through\n      divergent mechanisms\"。每增加一层attention，aggregate表现更相似，但每个架构处理的样本更不同。\n      这是一个genuine empirical paradox，即使scope限定在LAMBADA上，the finding itself is intellectually interesting\n      enough for Findings。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9617,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9617},"output_tokens":23,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5d2e06b4-f4d5-422a-a624-6c6aadf43447","uuid":"b0835e27-2345-49d7-b220-714a9f97239b"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":209027,"duration_api_ms":210405,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Claim 1收窄为\"retrieval-dependent tasks上的convergence\"，不再claim泛化性。\n  Claim 2从\"scale-dependent convergence\"改为\"binary contrast: 340M insufficient vs 1.3B sufficient\"，\n  承认无法建立完整scale law但指出threshold现象。\n  Claim 3（paradox）仍是核心卖点，但限定在LAMBADA上做深度案例研究。\n  Title加限定词如\"on retrieval-dependent tasks\"。目标：EMNLP 2026 Findings（Main边缘）。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Cross-task convergence quantification\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      对6个benchmark在1.3B和340M上计算cross-architecture std随attention ratio的变化趋势，\n      Spearman相关检验，并按retrieval-dependent vs reasoning-dependent分类task。\n    expected_results:\n      lambada_std_h0_to_h8_1_3b: [0.024, 0.005]\n      lambada_spearman_rho_1_3b: -0.90\n      lambada_spearman_p_1_3b: 0.037\n      hellaswag_std_h0_to_h8_1_3b: [0.018, 0.011]\n      hellaswag_spearman_rho_1_3b: -0.82\n      hellaswag_spearman_p_1_3b: 0.089\n      arc_easy_std_h0_to_h8_1_3b: [0.015, 0.013]\n      arc_easy_spearman_rho_1_3b: -0.30\n      arc_easy_spearman_p_1_3b: 0.624\n      arc_challenge_std_h0_to_h8_1_3b: [0.022, 0.019]\n      arc_challenge_spearman_rho_1_3b: -0.10\n      arc_challenge_spearman_p_1_3b: 0.873\n      piqa_std_h0_to_h8_1_3b: [0.011, 0.010]\n      piqa_spearman_rho_1_3b: -0.20\n      piqa_spearman_p_1_3b: 0.747\n      winogrande_std_h0_to_h8_1_3b: [0.016, 0.014]\n      winogrande_spearman_rho_1_3b: -0.50\n      winogrande_spearman_p_1_3b: 0.391\n      tasks_with_p_lt_0_05: 1\n      tasks_with_p_lt_0_10: 2\n      lambada_std_reduction_pct: 79\n      hellaswag_std_reduction_pct: 39\n    result_rationale: >\n      LAMBADA是high retrieval demand的cloze task——模型必须从长context中\"检索\"关键信息来预测最后一个词。\n      加入attention后，所有架构都能更有效地执行这种long-range retrieval，因此各架构的性能天花板趋同，\n      cross-arch std显著下降（ρ=-0.90, p=0.037）。HellaSwag有一定的retrieval成分（需要从premise推断continuation），\n      但同时涉及commonsense reasoning，因此convergence趋势弱于LAMBADA（ρ=-0.82但p=0.089，刚好不够显著）。\n      ARC、PIQA、Winogrande主要考察reasoning和world knowledge，这些能力更依赖于base recurrence的训练质量而非\n      attention带来的retrieval能力提升，因此attention并不能消除架构间的固有差异，std几乎不变。\n      这构成了一个清晰的task-type dichotomy：retrieval-dependent tasks收敛，reasoning tasks不收敛。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 1: Cross-architecture std reduction by benchmark (1.3B scale)\"\n        columns: [\"Benchmark\", \"Task Type\", \"Std (h=0)\", \"Std (h=8)\", \"Reduction %\", \"Spearman ρ\", \"p-value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LAMBADA\", \"Retrieval\", \"0.024\", \"0.005\", \"79%\", \"-0.90\", \"0.037*\"]\n          - [\"HellaSwag\", \"Retrieval+Reasoning\", \"0.018\", \"0.011\", \"39%\", \"-0.82\", \"0.089†\"]\n          - [\"ARC-Easy\", \"Reasoning\", \"0.015\", \"0.013\", \"13%\", \"-0.30\", \"0.624\"]\n          - [\"ARC-Challenge\", \"Reasoning\", \"0.022\", \"0.019\", \"14%\", \"-0.10\", \"0.873\"]\n          - [\"PIQA\", \"Reasoning\", \"0.011\", \"0.010\", \"9%\", \"-0.20\", \"0.747\"]\n          - [\"WinoGrande\", \"Reasoning\", \"0.016\", \"0.014\", \"13%\", \"-0.50\", \"0.391\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 1: 6-panel grid，每个benchmark一个panel。x轴attention ratio (0,1,3,5,8)，y轴cross-arch std。LAMBADA panel展示清晰下降曲线，HellaSwag有弱下降趋势，其余4个基本flat。灰色shaded区域标注'retrieval-dependent zone'。\"\n    analysis: >\n      仅LAMBADA通过p<0.05显著性检验，HellaSwag在p<0.10边缘。这支持将Claim 1收窄为retrieval-dependent tasks。\n      Dichotomy本身是一个有意义的发现——说明attention的equalizer effect具有task-specificity，\n      而非universally homogenizing。论文叙事可以将此framing为\"attention selectively equalizes retrieval\n      but not reasoning\"，这比universal claim弱但更精确、更defensible。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark per-example analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      对1.3B模型在HellaSwag、ARC-easy、ARC-challenge上用--log_samples重新跑lm-eval，\n      提取per-example accuracy变化，计算sample-level convergence和cross-architecture helped/hurt overlap。\n    expected_results:\n      hellaswag_pairwise_jaccard_helped: 0.14\n      hellaswag_pairwise_jaccard_hurt: 0.11\n      hellaswag_net_effect_gdn: -0.008\n      hellaswag_net_effect_retnet: -0.003\n      hellaswag_net_effect_hgrn2: 0.012\n      hellaswag_symmetric_paradox_strength: \"weak\"\n      arc_easy_pairwise_jaccard_helped: 0.22\n      arc_easy_convergence_pattern: \"absent\"\n      arc_challenge_pairwise_jaccard_helped: 0.19\n      arc_challenge_convergence_pattern: \"absent\"\n      gpu_hours_used: 7.5\n    result_rationale: >\n      HellaSwag上per-example分析会显示一定程度的paradox——helped/hurt样本跨架构的Jaccard仍然较低（0.11-0.14），\n      说明不同架构在不同样本上受益/受损，但效果不如LAMBADA干净：(1) HellaSwag是4选1的multiple-choice，\n      accuracy是discrete的0/1，不像LAMBADA的连续logprob那样能捕捉细粒度变化，这导致noise更大；\n      (2) net effect的asymmetry不如LAMBADA对称——GDN和RetNet被hurt的程度不同，HGRN2被help的程度也较小，\n      paradox的\"symmetric but opposite\"叙事在HellaSwag上不够compelling。\n      ARC-easy和ARC-challenge因为aggregate level就没有convergence，per-example level自然也没有一致的pattern——\n      Jaccard偏高（0.19-0.22）反映的是随机重叠而非systematic pattern。\n      这个结果支持将paradox深度分析限定在LAMBADA，HellaSwag作为supporting evidence但不作为核心claim。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 2: Per-example overlap analysis across benchmarks (1.3B, h3→h8)\"\n        columns: [\"Benchmark\", \"Jaccard (helped)\", \"Jaccard (hurt)\", \"GDN net\", \"RetNet net\", \"HGRN2 net\", \"Paradox clarity\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LAMBADA\", \"0.08\", \"0.06\", \"-0.031\", \"-0.018\", \"+0.027\", \"Strong\"]\n          - [\"HellaSwag\", \"0.14\", \"0.11\", \"-0.008\", \"-0.003\", \"+0.012\", \"Weak\"]\n          - [\"ARC-Easy\", \"0.22\", \"0.20\", \"+0.002\", \"-0.005\", \"+0.001\", \"None\"]\n          - [\"ARC-Challenge\", \"0.19\", \"0.17\", \"-0.003\", \"+0.001\", \"-0.002\", \"None\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 2: 2×2 panel。上排LAMBADA和HellaSwag的upset plot展示helped/hurt样本跨架构的overlap；下排对应的net effect bar chart。LAMBADA panel颜色对比鲜明（GDN/RetNet红色hurt vs HGRN2绿色help），HellaSwag panel对比较弱。\"\n    analysis: >\n      HellaSwag提供了部分supporting evidence——Jaccard低于random baseline说明architecture-specificity存在，\n      但net effect不够对称，paradox叙事不clean。ARC两个task完全没有pattern。\n      实际操作：论文中LAMBADA做完整deep dive（主图+主表），HellaSwag放在supplementary作为partial replication，\n      ARC作为negative control说明effect的task-specificity。这比只有LAMBADA的单task故事更robust。\n\n  - name: \"7B model evaluation (if available)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      检查Wang et al. HuggingFace repos中7B模型的可用性。如果可用则评估，如果不可用则加强340M的two-scale分析。\n    expected_results:\n      gdn_7b_available: false\n      retnet_7b_available: true\n      hgrn2_7b_available: false\n      complete_7b_trio: false\n      fallback_triggered: true\n      fallback_action: \"strengthen 2-scale binary contrast analysis\"\n      scale_points_available: 2\n    result_rationale: >\n      Wang et al.的model zoo主要集中在340M和1.3B规模——7B训练需要显著更多compute（约8×），\n      他们可能只对部分架构训练了7B。RetNet因为是相对成熟的架构（微软支持），最可能有7B版本，\n      但GDN和HGRN2作为较新的架构，7B训练可能未完成或未release。\n      只有一个架构的7B数据无法计算cross-architecture std，因此无法构成三点scale curve。\n      Fallback策略：将Claim 2重新框架为binary contrast——340M是\"insufficient scale\"（convergence partial，\n      有rebound），1.3B是\"sufficient scale\"（convergence complete）。这不是一个scale law，\n      而是一个threshold observation。叙事上诚实承认\"we cannot establish the full scaling trajectory\"，\n      但指出threshold的存在本身有practical implications（practitioners知道1.3B足够触发convergence）。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 3（修改版）: 不再画三点scale curve，而是side-by-side的两个panel——340M和1.3B各一个，每个panel内画cross-arch std vs attention ratio。用箭头和annotation标注'partial convergence with rebound'(340M) vs 'complete convergence'(1.3B)。\"\n    analysis: >\n      7B不可用是median tier最大的narrative限制。无法用三点建立scale law意味着Claim 2从quantitative scaling claim\n      降级为qualitative threshold observation。但binary contrast本身在empirical paper中是可接受的——\n      关键是要坦诚acknowledge limitation并在discussion中指出7B验证是important future work。\n      如果RetNet单独有7B，可以在appendix中报告\"single-architecture 7B data point consistent with trend\"，\n      但不能claim cross-architecture convergence at 7B。\n\n  - name: \"340M rebound mechanism analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007\"\n    description: >\n      深入分析340M在attn=8时的non-monotonic rebound——per-example比较340M与1.3B在相同attention ratio下的行为差异。\n    expected_results:\n      rebound_magnitude_std_increase_h5_to_h8: 0.008\n      rebound_primary_source: \"GDN disproportionate degradation at h=8\"\n      rebound_sample_overlap_with_1_3b_hurt: 0.35\n      capacity_limitation_hypothesis_support: \"moderate\"\n      gdn_340m_h8_accuracy_drop_vs_h5: -0.028\n      retnet_340m_h8_accuracy_drop_vs_h5: -0.009\n      hgrn2_340m_h8_accuracy_change_vs_h5: +0.004\n      identified_mechanism: \"capacity bottleneck — at 340M, replacing too many recurrent layers with attention leaves insufficient recurrent capacity for sequence modeling, hitting GDN hardest due to its higher recurrent parameter efficiency\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      340M模型的total parameter budget有限。当attention ratio从h=5增加到h=8时，大量recurrent层被替换为attention层。\n      在1.3B规模下，剩余的recurrent层仍有足够capacity处理sequence modeling，但在340M下，\n      recurrent层的capacity被过度压缩。GDN的gated delta rule机制对参数效率最敏感——\n      它依赖于gate和delta的精确交互，参数减少导致这种交互退化最严重。\n      RetNet基于exponential decay的机制相对robust但也受影响。HGRN2的hierarchical结构天然对capacity减少有一定resilience。\n      Per-example分析中，340M rebound处受影响的样本与1.3B被hurt的样本overlap只有0.35——\n      说明rebound不是简单的\"same problem at smaller scale\"，而是340M特有的capacity limitation触发了不同failure mode。\n      这个解释合理但缺乏formal quantitative validation（如information bottleneck分析），因此标注为\"moderate support\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 3: 340M rebound decomposition (h=5 → h=8)\"\n        columns: [\"Architecture\", \"Acc@h5\", \"Acc@h8\", \"Δ\", \"Cross-arch std contribution\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GDN\", \"0.412\", \"0.384\", \"-0.028\", \"↑ major\"]\n          - [\"RetNet\", \"0.398\", \"0.389\", \"-0.009\", \"↑ minor\"]\n          - [\"HGRN2\", \"0.405\", \"0.409\", \"+0.004\", \"↓ minor\"]\n          - [\"Cross-arch std\", \"0.007\", \"0.013\", \"+0.006\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 4: 左panel为340M三架构accuracy随attention ratio的曲线，h=8处GDN明显下弯；右panel为scatter plot展示340M rebound样本vs 1.3B hurt样本的overlap（low Jaccard）。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Capacity limitation假设提供了合理解释但不是定量严格的。论文中将此作为\"interesting secondary finding\"处理——\n      在Results中用一小节描述，在Discussion中作为evidence支持\"convergence requires sufficient scale\"的论点。\n      不过不要过度claim因果关系，用\"consistent with\"而非\"demonstrates\"的语言。\n\n  - name: \"Helped/hurt sample characterization\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      对LAMBADA上各架构的helped/hurt样本计算target token frequency、context length、last-sentence complexity等特征，\n      检验是否有显著差异。\n    expected_results:\n      target_token_frequency_p_value_helped_vs_hurt: 0.003\n      target_token_frequency_effect_direction: \"hurt samples have lower-frequency target tokens\"\n      target_token_frequency_cohens_d: 0.38\n      context_length_p_value_helped_vs_hurt: 0.12\n      context_length_effect_direction: \"weak trend — hurt samples slightly longer\"\n      last_sentence_perplexity_p_value: 0.067\n      cross_architecture_feature_difference_significant: true\n      gdn_hurt_skew: \"low-frequency targets with medium context\"\n      retnet_hurt_skew: \"low-frequency targets with long context\"\n      hgrn2_helped_skew: \"low-frequency targets across context lengths\"\n      significant_features_count: 1\n      marginally_significant_features_count: 1\n    result_rationale: >\n      Target token frequency是最可能显著的特征，因为retrieval-dependent prediction的核心难度在于target token的可预测性。\n      低频词更难预测，attention的加入对不同架构在这类样本上的影响不同：\n      - GDN的delta rule机制擅长精确的key-value关联，加入attention后在低频目标上反而产生interference（两种attention机制竞争）\n      - RetNet的exponential decay对长distance retrieval本来就弱，attention在长context+低频target上无法完全补偿\n      - HGRN2的hierarchical gating从attention中获益最多，因为它的base mechanism最缺乏long-range retrieval能力\n      Context length效果不显著（p=0.12）可能因为LAMBADA样本的context length变化范围有限（多数在50-200 tokens之间），\n      不足以产生统计显著的差异。Last-sentence perplexity在边缘（p=0.067）。\n      Cross-architecture差异在target frequency上显著——三个架构的hurt样本都倾向low-frequency targets，\n      但具体的frequency threshold和与context length的交互pattern不同，这解释了为什么Jaccard低。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 4: Sample feature analysis — helped vs hurt on LAMBADA (1.3B, h0→h8)\"\n        columns: [\"Feature\", \"Helped mean\", \"Hurt mean\", \"Cohen's d\", \"p-value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Target token log-freq\", \"-5.2\", \"-6.8\", \"0.38\", \"0.003**\"]\n          - [\"Context length (tokens)\", \"87.3\", \"94.1\", \"0.15\", \"0.12\"]\n          - [\"Last-sent perplexity\", \"42.1\", \"51.8\", \"0.21\", \"0.067†\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 5: 三行（GDN/RetNet/HGRN2）×两列（target freq distribution / context length distribution）的violin plot。Helped样本蓝色，hurt样本红色。Target frequency列上三架构都显示shift但shift pattern不同。\"\n    analysis: >\n      仅1个特征（target token frequency）达到strong significance，1个marginally significant。这符合median tier预期。\n      Target frequency作为单一显著特征足以构成一个coherent story：attention的equalizer effect主要作用在\n      低频target token的retrieval上，但不同架构对这类样本的处理策略不同。\n      论文中可以用这个结果支持Claim 3的mechanistic interpretation——\"convergence through complementary mechanisms\"\n      有了具体的linguistic grounding（不同架构在不同frequency regime的低频tokens上diverge）。\n      Limitation：只有1-2个显著特征意味着mechanistic story不够多维度，reviewer可能要求更多特征。\n      准备rebuttal：(a) LAMBADA样本本身的feature空间较窄，(b) frequency是retrieval task最relevant的特征。\n\n  - name: \"Attention weight extraction and visualization\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: >\n      提取三个架构hybrid model (h3-1 config)的attention weight，分析attention pattern与per-example effect的关系。\n    expected_results:\n      attention_pattern_similarity_gdn_retnet: 0.42\n      attention_pattern_similarity_gdn_hgrn2: 0.31\n      attention_pattern_similarity_retnet_hgrn2: 0.38\n      correlation_attention_entropy_with_helped: 0.28\n      correlation_attention_focus_position_with_effect: 0.33\n      qualitative_finding: \"GDN attention concentrates on recent context; RetNet distributes more uniformly; HGRN2 shows bimodal pattern with peaks at sentence boundaries\"\n      gpu_hours_used: 3.5\n    result_rationale: >\n      三种base recurrence机制对信息的编码方式不同，这会影响attention层\"看到\"的hidden states的distribution，\n      进而导致不同的attention pattern。GDN通过delta rule维护explicit key-value memory，\n      attention层在这个基础上倾向于做local refinement（集中在recent context）；\n      RetNet的exponential decay平滑了positional信息，attention分布更uniform；\n      HGRN2的hierarchical gating创造了sentence-boundary处的natural segmentation，\n      attention倾向于在这些boundary处聚焦。\n      Attention entropy与helped/hurt的相关性中等（r=0.28-0.33），因为attention weight只是机制的一个proxy，\n      实际效果还取决于value vector的内容和后续层的处理。\n      这些相关性达不到pass_fail threshold（>0.3）的一部分，但focus position的相关性（0.33）刚好过线。\n      整体来说提供了supportive但非conclusive的mechanistic evidence。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 5: Cross-architecture attention pattern analysis (h3-1, 1.3B)\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"GDN\", \"RetNet\", \"HGRN2\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Mean attention entropy\", \"1.82\", \"2.45\", \"2.11\"]\n          - [\"% attention on last 20 tokens\", \"48%\", \"29%\", \"35%\"]\n          - [\"Correlation with helped (r)\", \"0.28\", \"0.25\", \"0.33\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 6: 三个architecture的average attention heatmap（x轴=query position, y轴=key position），各展示不同的attention pattern。下方bar chart展示与per-example effect的correlation。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Attention pattern分析提供了定性的mechanistic支持——三个架构确实展现出不同的attention策略，\n      与per-example divergence的发现一致。但相关性不够强，不足以claim causal mechanism。\n      论文中放在supplementary或作为一个小节提供visual evidence，不作为核心argument。\n      这对median tier来说是合适的——有一些mechanistic insight但不deep enough for a full claim。\n\n  - name: \"Architecture expansion check\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      搜索Wang et al. model zoo和其他source寻找额外的hybrid architectures（Mamba/Mamba2, RWKV等），\n      评估convergence是否泛化。\n    expected_results:\n      mamba2_hybrid_found: false\n      rwkv_hybrid_found: false\n      additional_architectures_evaluated: 0\n      wang_et_al_architectures_confirmed: [\"GDN\", \"RetNet\", \"HGRN2\"]\n      other_sources_checked: [\"HuggingFace Hub\", \"Papers with Code\", \"GitHub\"]\n      conclusion: \"no additional comparable hybrid architectures available with matching scale/ratio configurations\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Wang et al.的model zoo是目前最全面的hybrid architecture比较资源。他们选择的三个架构（GDN, RetNet, HGRN2）\n      已经覆盖了主要的linear recurrence类型。Mamba/Mamba2的hybrid版本虽然存在于一些研究中，\n      但没有以相同的scale（340M/1.3B）和attention ratio（0,1,3,5,8层）系统训练并release的checkpoint。\n      RWKV hybrid更是一个新兴方向，公开的comparable checkpoints几乎没有。\n      这意味着我们stuck在n=3架构——但这三个架构确实代表了三种不同的recurrence mechanism，\n      不是arbitrary的架构选择。论文中需要在limitation section说明这一点。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      无法扩展架构数量。Mitigation：(1) 在方法论上强调三个架构代表三类不同的recurrence paradigm，\n      (2) 引用Wang et al.选择这三个架构的justification，(3) 在limitation中explicitly call out n=3，\n      (4) 指出每个架构×5 ratios×2 scales的per-example analysis提供了thousands of data points。\n      对于EMNLP Findings来说，n=3但per-example analysis deep的paper是可接受的。\n\n  - name: \"Statistical robustness framework\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      Bootstrap CI、多重比较校正、排除GDN的sensitivity analysis、effect sizes。\n    expected_results:\n      bootstrap_ci_lambada_std_reduction_95: [0.004, 0.021]\n      bootstrap_ci_lower_bound_positive: true\n      bootstrap_ci_hellaswag_std_reduction_95: [-0.002, 0.015]\n      bootstrap_ci_hellaswag_lower_crosses_zero: true\n      bonferroni_corrected_p_lambada: 0.222\n      fdr_corrected_p_lambada: 0.074\n      fdr_corrected_p_hellaswag: 0.267\n      gdn_excluded_lambada_spearman_rho: -0.80\n      gdn_excluded_lambada_spearman_p: 0.133\n      gdn_excluded_bootstrap_ci_std_reduction: [0.001, 0.018]\n      gdn_excluded_ci_crosses_zero: false\n      cohens_d_lambada_convergence: 0.72\n      eta_squared_attention_ratio_effect: 0.41\n    result_rationale: >\n      Bootstrap CI对LAMBADA的std reduction不跨零（[0.004, 0.021]），确认convergence是real的。\n      但CI相当宽，反映了n=3架构带来的有限统计power。\n      HellaSwag的bootstrap CI跨零（[-0.002, 0.015]），与exp-001中p=0.089一致——borderline。\n      Bonferroni correction对6个benchmarks（×6）后LAMBADA的p值从0.037变为0.222——不再显著。\n      但FDR correction（less conservative）给出0.074，接近显著。这里的tension需要在论文中诚实讨论——\n      如果用strict Bonferroni全都不显著，但Bonferroni在correlated tests上过于conservative。\n      FDR更appropriate但仍只是borderline。解决方案：focus on LAMBADA的pre-registered hypothesis（不需correction），\n      其他tasks作为exploratory analysis用FDR。\n      排除GDN后：direction保持（ρ=-0.80）但p值变大（0.133），因为只剩两个架构（RetNet, HGRN2），\n      permutation test的resolution有限。关键是bootstrap CI仍不跨零（[0.001, 0.018]）——\n      CI下界接近零但还是正的，说明convergence方向在没有GDN的情况下依然成立，只是不够显著。\n      Cohen's d=0.72属于medium-to-large effect，说明convergence不是trivial的。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 6: Statistical robustness summary\"\n        columns: [\"Analysis\", \"LAMBADA\", \"HellaSwag\", \"Others\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Raw Spearman p\", \"0.037*\", \"0.089†\", \">0.39\"]\n          - [\"Bonferroni-corrected p\", \"0.222\", \"0.534\", \">1.0\"]\n          - [\"FDR-corrected p\", \"0.074†\", \"0.267\", \">0.58\"]\n          - [\"Bootstrap 95% CI (std reduction)\", \"[0.004, 0.021]\", \"[-0.002, 0.015]\", \"all cross zero\"]\n          - [\"GDN-excluded bootstrap CI\", \"[0.001, 0.018]\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Cohen's d\", \"0.72\", \"0.34\", \"<0.2\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 7: Forest plot展示各benchmark的bootstrap CI。LAMBADA的CI在正区间，HellaSwag刚好跨零，其余clearly跨零。右侧panel展示GDN-excluded的sensitivity analysis CI。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Robustness analysis的结论是nuanced的：LAMBADA的convergence是robust的（CI不跨零，medium-large effect size），\n      但statistical significance在multiple comparison correction后变弱。\n      排除GDN后direction preserved但CI下界接近零——这是honest reporting，reviewer会appreciate这种transparency。\n      论文策略：(1) Pre-register LAMBADA为primary hypothesis，avoid multiple comparison问题，\n      (2) 报告FDR而非Bonferroni（justification：tasks are correlated），\n      (3) GDN sensitivity作为robustness check而非primary analysis，\n      (4) 强调effect size（d=0.72）而非仅rely on p-value。\n      这种nuanced statistical picture对EMNLP Findings是sufficient的——不pretend effect比实际更强。\n\n  - name: \"Wang et al. explicit differentiation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      正式的side-by-side比较：Wang et al.报告了什么，我们的分析新增了什么。\n    expected_results:\n      wang_convergence_statements_found: 2\n      wang_statement_1: \"qualitative observation that hybrid models show similar performance at higher attention ratios\"\n      wang_statement_2: \"aggregate benchmark tables showing decreasing variance (not explicitly computed or tested)\"\n      differentiation_point_1: \"We compute cross-architecture std trajectories with statistical tests — they don't\"\n      differentiation_point_2: \"We perform per-example analysis revealing the equalizer paradox — they don't\"\n      differentiation_point_3: \"We characterize scale dependency of convergence (340M partial vs 1.3B complete) — they don't\"\n      differentiation_point_4: \"We provide mechanistic analysis linking sample features to architecture-specific effects — they don't\"\n      wang_overlap_risk: \"moderate — a reviewer familiar with their paper will see the qualitative convergence trend in their tables\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Wang et al.的论文focus是建model zoo和benchmark hybrid architectures的aggregate performance。\n      他们在论文中很可能提到了\"increasing attention leads to similar performance across architectures\"\n      作为一个observation，但没有将其作为核心finding来quantify或analyze。\n      他们的Table/Figure中确实隐含了convergence趋势（读者可以从数字中看出来），但他们没有：\n      (a) 计算cross-arch std并测试其与attention ratio的关系，\n      (b) 做任何per-example分析，\n      (c) 区分不同scale下convergence的不同程度，\n      (d) 分析为什么convergence发生。\n      Risk在于reviewer可能认为\"convergence observation已经在Wang et al.中了\"——mitigation是\n      明确acknowledge他们的qualitative observation并frame our contribution为将这个observation\n      从qualitative提升到quantitative+mechanistic。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 7: Differentiation from Wang et al. (2025)\"\n        columns: [\"Analysis dimension\", \"Wang et al.\", \"Our work\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Convergence observation\", \"Qualitative (implicit in tables)\", \"Quantitative (Spearman tests, effect sizes)\"]\n          - [\"Per-example analysis\", \"None\", \"Helped/hurt decomposition, Jaccard overlap\"]\n          - [\"Scale dependency\", \"Not analyzed\", \"340M partial vs 1.3B complete, rebound mechanism\"]\n          - [\"Mechanistic analysis\", \"None\", \"Sample characterization, attention pattern analysis\"]\n          - [\"Statistical framework\", \"None\", \"Bootstrap CI, sensitivity analysis, multiple comparison\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Differentiation清晰但需要careful framing。在Introduction中：acknowledge Wang et al.的model zoo贡献，\n      然后explicit说\"building on their excellent resource, we discover and characterize...\"。\n      在Related Work中：detailed comparison table。避免任何暗示他们\"missed\"something的语言——\n      frame为\"their focus was X, ours is complementary Y\"。\n      Risk assessment：如果Wang et al.的reviewer也review我们的paper（likely given community size），\n      他们可能defensive。Respectful framing essential。\n\n  - name: \"Convergence-divergence bridge analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-010\"\n    description: >\n      在LAMBADA上同时plot aggregate convergence和per-example divergence metrics，展示paradox的co-evolution。\n    expected_results:\n      correlation_aggregate_std_vs_jaccard: -0.88\n      correlation_p_value: 0.048\n      aggregate_std_trajectory: [0.024, 0.019, 0.012, 0.008, 0.005]\n      mean_pairwise_jaccard_trajectory: [0.15, 0.12, 0.10, 0.08, 0.07]\n      net_effect_asymmetry_trajectory: [0.008, 0.015, 0.021, 0.025, 0.031]\n      paradox_intensification_with_attention: true\n      effect_asymmetry_correlation_with_attention_ratio: 0.95\n    result_rationale: >\n      随着attention ratio增加，aggregate convergence加强（std下降）同时per-example divergence也在加强\n      （Jaccard下降、net effect asymmetry增加）。这是因为更多的attention层给了每个架构更大的\"空间\"\n      来发展architecture-specific的processing策略——base recurrence mechanism决定了哪些sample被route到attention，\n      而更多的attention层意味着这种architecture-specific routing的影响被放大。\n      Aggregate convergence的同时出现是因为这些不同策略恰好\"平均化\"到similar的overall performance——\n      这不是coincidence而是因为attention的通用retrieval能力设定了一个performance ceiling，\n      不同架构通过不同路径reach这个ceiling。\n      Correlation为-0.88（p=0.048）——刚好显著。这是paradox的quantitative visualization。\n      Net effect asymmetry（|GDN_net| + |RetNet_net| + |HGRN2_net|）随attention ratio单调增加，\n      correlation 0.95——说明per-example effects变得更pronounced even as aggregate converges。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 8: Convergence-divergence co-evolution on LAMBADA (1.3B)\"\n        columns: [\"Attention layers\", \"Cross-arch std\", \"Mean pairwise Jaccard\", \"Net effect asymmetry\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"0 (pure recurrent)\", \"0.024\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"1\", \"0.019\", \"0.12\", \"0.015\"]\n          - [\"3\", \"0.012\", \"0.10\", \"0.021\"]\n          - [\"5\", \"0.008\", \"0.08\", \"0.025\"]\n          - [\"8\", \"0.005\", \"0.07\", \"0.031\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 8 (论文核心图): Dual-axis plot。左y轴为cross-arch std（下降曲线，蓝色），右y轴为net effect asymmetry（上升曲线，红色）。x轴为attention层数。两条曲线形成'X'形交叉，视觉化paradox。下方small multiples展示各attention ratio下的pairwise Jaccard heatmap逐渐变冷（overlap减少）。\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是论文的\"money figure\"——一张图capture整个paradox。Dual-axis plot清晰展示aggregate convergence和\n      per-example divergence的co-evolution。Correlation显著（p=0.048）但不是overwhelmingly strong，\n      符合median tier。\n      Narrative：这张图支撑整个Section 4（或5）的核心argument——\"attention creates convergence through\n      divergent mechanisms\"。每增加一层attention，aggregate表现更相似，但每个架构处理的样本更不同。\n      这是一个genuine empirical paradox，即使scope限定在LAMBADA上，the finding itself is intellectually interesting\n      enough for Findings。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"5d2e06b4-f4d5-422a-a624-6c6aadf43447","total_cost_usd":0.33278375000000004,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9617,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":10483,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9617,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":10483,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9617,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9617},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":4577,"outputTokens":19,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.004672,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":10483,"cacheReadInputTokens":11841,"cacheCreationInputTokens":9617,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.32811175000000004,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"acf8fb5f-6cfe-404b-ba70-763bc54c1396"}
